# Line endings are pinned to LF, everywhere, for everyone.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true on init, which would rewrite this
# whole working copy to CRLF the first time git touched it - a full-file diff
# on every file, hiding the one line that actually changed. There is no build
# step here: the file that is edited is the file that is served, so it should
# be byte-identical on every machine that checks it out.
#
# index.html deliberately contains no unprintable characters - the combining
# accents and the byte-order mark are built with String.fromCharCode precisely
# so nothing invisible can be mangled in transit. Pinning eol keeps that
# promise across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.csv -text
